             'activists_strength', 'georgia_survives', 'renounced_armed', 'spring_won', 'no_terror',
             'martov_line', 'war_aims_note', 'bol_unity', 'soviet_power_motion', 'reconvene_assembly',
             'ca_extra', 'prisoners_freed', 'steinberg_line', 'constitution', 'dissent_dummy',
             'land_law_draft', 'peasant_organised', 'army_raised', 'komuch_alive', 'chernov_gov', 'lsr_kept', 'ufa_line',
             'lsr_in_gov', 'lsr_seats', 'lsr_backs_bol', 'lsr_survives', 'split_planned', 'cheka_shield', 'seven_commissars', 'lsr_squeezed',
             'kolchak_seen', 'land_socialised', 'prog_rb', 'prog_po', 'cheka_seats', 'lsr_rising', 'anti_brest', 'early_split', 'blocs', 'bloc_lean', 'dissent_extra',
             'turmoil_men', 'turmoil_sr', 'turmoil_lsr', 'turmoil_bol', 'komuch_averted', 'lsr_uprising_averted',
             'split_alliance_done', 'anti_brest_front', 'lent_chernov', 'lent_dan', 'lent_spiridonova', 'lent_martov',
             'ant_kad', 'ant_gen', 'ant_bol', 'opp_kad_ev', 'opp_gen_ev', 'opp_bol_ev', 'opp_kad_n', 'opp_gen_n', 'opp_bol_n',
             'opp_kad_age', 'opp_gen_age', 'opp_bol_age', 'opp_kad_base', 'opp_gen_base', 'opp_bol_base'];
Q.fault_text = '';
Q.fault_flag = 0;
// standing policies of the Cabinet: land, food, war, order, labour (food starts at the grain monopoly)
Q.pol_land = 0;
Q.pol_food = 1;
Q.pol_war = 0;
Q.pol_order = 0;
Q.pol_labour = 0;
Q.pol_finance = 0;
for (var fl of flags) { Q[fl] = 0; }
Q.dues_income = 1;

// records
Q.polls_enabled = 1;
RO.clampStats(Q);
RO.updateFactions(Q);
RO.updatePolls(Q);
RO.display(Q);
!}
new-page: true

= Choose your party

The February Revolution has overthrown the Tsar. Three socialist parties stand outside Lenin's Bolsheviks and, in March 1917, none of them is in power. Each has its own base, its own quarrels and its own road.

- @pick_men: The Mensheviks. Russia's social democrats, with their strength among the workers and railwaymen. *Hard.*
- @pick_sr: The Socialist Revolutionaries. The largest party in Russia, the party of the peasants and the soldiers. *Normal.*
- @pick_lsr: The Left SRs. The left wing of the SR party, which does not yet exist as a party: the peasants' radicals, the Baltic sailors. *Hard.*

@pick_men
on-arrival: {!
RO.initParty(Q, 'menshevik');
RO.updateFactions(Q); RO.updatePolls(Q); RO.display(Q);
!}
go-to: difficulty

@pick_sr
on-arrival: {!
RO.initParty(Q, 'sr');
RO.updateFactions(Q); RO.updatePolls(Q); RO.display(Q);
!}
go-to: difficulty

@pick_lsr
on-arrival: {!
RO.initParty(Q, 'lsr');
RO.updateFactions(Q); RO.updatePolls(Q); RO.display(Q);
!}
go-to: difficulty

@difficulty
new-page: true

= Choose your difficulty

- @easy: Easy. More resources, a bigger hand, cards can be returned, and the currents, the opposition and the generals are a little gentler.
- @normal: Normal.
- @hard: Hard. Fewer resources, no returning cards, currents that are harder to hold together, an opposition that angers faster, and stronger generals.

@easy
on-arrival: {!
Q.difficulty = -1; Q.resources += 2; Q.hand_size = 4;
for (var f of Q.factions) { Q[f + '_dissent'] = Math.round(Q[f + '_dissent'] * 0.5); }
RO.updateFactions(Q);
!}
go-to: intro

@normal
on-arrival: difficulty = 0;
go-to: intro

@hard
on-arrival: {!
Q.difficulty = 1; Q.resources = Math.max(0, Q.resources - 2); Q.discard_disabled = 1;
for (var f of Q.factions) { Q[f + '_dissent'] += 10; }
Q.rel_ally -= 10;
RO.updateFactions(Q);
!}
go-to: intro

@intro
new-page: true
go-to: intro_men if player_party = 'menshevik'; intro_sr if player_party = 'sr'; intro_lsr if player_party = 'lsr'

@intro_men
new-page: true
go-to: intro_common

= March 1917

> *"The Russian revolution is a bourgeois revolution; it can only be a bourgeois revolution, and the democratic bourgeoisie must lead it."*
>
> The Menshevik reading of 1917 (paraphrased)

The February Revolution has overthrown the monarchy. A Provisional Government of liberals sits in the Tauride Palace, and in the same building a Soviet of Workers' and Soldiers' Deputies, led by Mensheviks and Socialist Revolutionaries, holds the real power: the garrison, the railways and the telegraph obey the Soviet, not the ministers.

Your party has an unusual task. It is Russia's social democracy, in the same International as the German SPD, and it believes that Russia is not ready for socialism. It wants a democratic republic, the end of the war on fair terms, and room for workers to organise. Its rivals say that this is the road to disaster.

@intro_sr
new-page: true
go-to: intro_common

= March 1917

> *"In struggle you will win your right."*
>
> The motto of the Socialist Revolutionary Party

The February Revolution has overthrown the monarchy. A Provisional Government of liberals sits in the Tauride Palace, and in the same building a Soviet of Workers' and Soldiers' Deputies, led by Socialist Revolutionaries and Mensheviks, holds the real power: the garrison, the railways and the telegraph obey the Soviet, not the ministers. One of your own, the lawyer Kerensky, sits in the cabinet.

Your party is the largest in Russia. In a few months it will have close to a million members, and the votes of most of the peasants and soldiers. It wants the land for those who work it, socialised and not divided; it wants a democratic republic, and a Constituent Assembly to found it. It is also as divided as it is large: the Right SRs (Avksentiev, Breshko-Breshkovskaya), the Centre (Chernov), the Right Centre (Gots, Zenzinov) and the Left SRs (Spiridonova, Kamkov), who think the party has already betrayed the peasants.

@intro_lsr
new-page: true
go-to: intro_common

= March 1917

> *"The land belongs to those who work it."*
>
> The Left SR slogan

The February Revolution has overthrown the monarchy. A Provisional Government of liberals sits in the Tauride Palace, and in the same building a Soviet of Workers' and Soldiers' Deputies, led by Socialist Revolutionaries and Mensheviks, holds the real power. One of the SRs, Kerensky, is in the cabinet.

You lead the left wing of the SR party: the peasants' radicals, who say that the party has forgotten the land; the opponents of the war, who say that the party has forgotten the peace; the sailors of Kronstadt and the Baltic Fleet, who say that the Soviet should take all power. You are Spiridonova, Kamkov, Natanson: the old terrorists and the old populists. You are not yet a party. You are a faction of the largest party in Russia, a faction that shares its name, its newspaper and its voters. Whether to break with it, and when, is the most important decision that you will make.

@intro_common

Every two weeks you will play a card: a meeting, a campaign, a ministry, an advisor's advice. Between cards, history happens. You lead the party until December 1921. You can lose it to a counter-revolution of the Right, to a Bolshevik one-party state, or to exile. Or you can save something of what was won in February.

*This is a game of alternate history. The dates are given in the New Style (Gregorian) calendar; before February 1918 Russia kept the Old Style, thirteen days behind.*

*Red October is a work in progress.*

- @post_event: Begin.
